# VERIDIQ_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Clerk — primary browser sign-in/up via @clerk/clerk-react; FastAPI JWT still issued after sync
# https://clerk.com/docs
# https://clerk.com/docs/deployments/overview
#
# KEY MODES (do not invent keys — copy from Clerk Dashboard → API Keys):
#   Development instance → pk_test_… / sk_test_…
#     - Correct for local Vite (5173) + FastAPI. Clerk will warn about "development keys"
#       and that you cannot deploy that instance to production — expected, not a bug.
#   Production instance  → pk_live_… / sk_live_…
#     - Required before any real production deploy. Create a Production instance in Clerk,
#       then replace ALL of the keys below (Vite + server). Never commit live secrets.
#
# Publishable (safe for Vite): set BOTH to the same publishable key
# VERIDIQ_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
# VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
# Secret (server only — never expose to Vite / never prefix with VITE_)
# VERIDIQ_CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# Optional override if publishable-key decode fails:
# VERIDIQ_CLERK_FRONTEND_API=your-instance.clerk.accounts.dev
# Clerk Dashboard → Configure → Domains / Paths:
#   Allowed origins: http://127.0.0.1:5173 , http://localhost:5173
#   Sign-in URL: /sign-in   Sign-up URL: /sign-up
# Web3 / MetaMask: ENABLE in Clerk Dashboard → User & Authentication → Web3
#   → turn ON MetaMask. The /sign-in and /sign-up pages show the MetaMask button
#   when this is on. Users need the MetaMask browser extension
#   (https://metamask.io/download/). Google + email remain available either way.
#   If Web3 is off in the Dashboard, the MetaMask button will not appear
#   (Clerk controls which social/Web3 methods render).
# Stripe — server needs sk_test_/sk_live_ (pk_ alone is not enough)
# VERIDIQ_STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# VERIDIQ_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# If a non-sk/pk value was pasted, store for review only:
# VERIDIQ_STRIPE_KEY_RAW=
# Firebase — project id alone is configuration_required until service account
# VERIDIQ_FIREBASE_PROJECT=
# VERIDIQ_FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=
# Slack bot token (xoxb-...)
# VERIDIQ_SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=
# Discord bot token
# VERIDIQ_DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=
# Playwright browser automation (opt-in)
# VERIDIQ_BROWSER_RUNTIME=0
# WebRTC signaling is internal (no key). Twilio Voice still gates PSTN dials.

